{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwgKKwg3bPsNG27mBqT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For [Co(ox)₃]³⁻, **Dq ≈ 1856 cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 18 557 cm⁻¹), B ≈ 432 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 1946 cm⁻¹**. These come from the standard strong-field (first-order) expressions for low-spin octahedral d⁶.\n\n**Band energies in the strong-field limit**\n\nThe ground state of low-spin d⁶ is ¹A₁g. The two spin-allowed transitions are:\n\n- ¹A₁g → ¹T₁g: E₁ = 10Dq − C\n- ¹A₁g → ¹T₂g: E₂ = 10Dq + 16B − C\n\n**Solving for B**\n\nSubtracting the first band from the second removes both Dq and C:\n\nE₂ − E₁ = 16B = 23 529 − 16 611 = 6918 cm⁻¹\n\nB = 6918 / 16 = **432.4 cm⁻¹**\n\n**Finding C**\n\nC = 4.5B = 4.5 × 432.4 = **1945.7 cm⁻¹**\n\n**Finding Dq**\n\n10Dq = E₁ + C = 16 611 + 1945.7 = 18 556.7 cm⁻¹\n\nDq = **1855.7 cm⁻¹**\n\n**Limitations**\n\n- The strong-field formulas ignore configuration mixing (the second-order B²/10Dq terms), so these values are approximate.\n- C is not determined from the spectrum. It follows only from the assumed ratio C/B = 4.5, so Dq depends on that assumption as well.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1855.7, \"B\": 432.4, \"C\": 1945.7, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Solved strong-field low-spin d6 expressions 10Dq−C and 10Dq+16B−C with C=4.5B.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":820,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6db285cf-6b01-4dae-8111-c62149696d75","uuid":"6db8781f-7023-4df5-8ade-2dec7d7d256b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:10:48.237Z","request_id":"req_011CghwgJybuGTVLyEPp8RqB"}
